CloudSim Simulation and Custom Scheduling
Cloud Computing Lab Exam Notes

Covers the four supplied question-bank tasks: create a basic CloudSim simulation; run multiple VMs/cloudlets and show makespan; implement a custom scheduling algorithm; compare a custom policy with a baseline policy.

1. What you need

CloudSim is a Java-based simulation toolkit. It does not create real cloud servers; it simulates datacenters, hosts, virtual machines, cloudlets (jobs), and scheduling.

Use the CloudSim version supplied by your instructor. The code below targets the classic CloudSim 3.x API (org.cloudbus.cloudsim.*). CloudSim Plus uses a different API, so these examples may need adaptation if your lab uses CloudSim Plus.

